From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: waydroid-nvidia-prolapse <build@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:58:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/20] hwcomposer: ignore SIGPIPE in the composer process

What: signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN) at the start of hwc_open().

Why: SIGPIPE's default action terminates the composer with no tombstone and
no log line from us (init only reports "received signal 13"), and
SurfaceFlinger and zygote restart behind it. The writers that can raise it
here are the input FIFOs /dev/input/wl_*_events (reader: system_server's
EventHub, which closes them whenever it restarts) and the clipboard transfer
pipe in data_source_handle_send() (reader: a host application that may close
it early). With SIGPIPE ignored those writes return EPIPE; the input writers
already log a failed write and work again once a new reader opens the FIFO.

Source: QuinOvaX, quinovax/waydroid-nvidia dev 1608854 / 74f7b93
  https://github.com/quinovax/waydroid-nvidia/commit/16088545af9a95423c8762baeb4b80f4a5dadc2a
  https://github.com/quinovax/waydroid-nvidia/commit/74f7b9308fa1d1e4e81fb52570735ed562ee3fc1
Licence: Apache-2.0 (android_hardware_waydroid; the fork's patches/hwcomposer/
inherit it).

Deviation from the source: same one-line fix; the rationale differs. The
source attributes the SIGPIPE to wl_display_flush()/roundtrip writes to the
compositor socket, but libwayland sends with MSG_NOSIGNAL (wayland 1.25.0
src/connection.c:494-495), so that socket cannot raise it; the FIFO and pipe
writers above can.
---
 hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
index 705bde3..7405148 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <pthread.h>
 #include <semaphore.h>
+#include <signal.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <sys/time.h>
 #include <sys/resource.h>
@@ -843,6 +844,16 @@ static int hwc_open(const struct hw_module_t* module, const char* name,
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
+    /* A write to a pipe or FIFO without a reader must fail with EPIPE, not kill the composer
+     * with SIGPIPE (default action: terminate, no tombstone, no log line from us). The writers
+     * here are the input FIFOs (/dev/input/wl_*_events, read by system_server's EventHub, which
+     * closes them when it restarts) and the clipboard transfer pipe (WaydroidClipboard.cpp,
+     * read by a host application that may close it early). The input writers log a failed
+     * write and succeed again once a new reader opens the FIFO; a failed clipboard write is a
+     * paste the host application abandoned. libwayland itself sends with
+     * MSG_NOSIGNAL, so the compositor socket never raised SIGPIPE. */
+    signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN);
+
     waydroid_hwc_composer_device_1 *pdev = new waydroid_hwc_composer_device_1();
     if (!pdev) {
         ALOGE("%s failed to allocate dev", __FUNCTION__);
